{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch73VvosRJXSy9AhaRvbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't include the guarantee that a gift this month places every child on the waiting list by January. The math doesn't support it:\n\n- **Cost of the full waiting list:** 61 × $1,150 = **$70,150**.\n- **Most the match can produce:** $30,000 ($15,000 in gifts plus $15,000 matched).\n- **If all 340 lapsed donors gave their average $85 and every dollar were matched:** about $57,800. That's still short, and last year this group gave $1,240.\n\nA promise you can't keep would also be risky with this group. Many of them left after Eastside closed and feel you already let them down once. The former board member forwards your emails with comments, and a broken guarantee is exactly what she'd point out. So the email shows what each gift buys and makes a smaller promise you can keep.\n\n**Check before sending:**\n- **The Eastside lines.** They admit the closure hurt without explaining why it happened. Your executive director should agree with them, since the email goes out under their name. If you're reopening or expanding anywhere, add a sentence about it here.\n- **The February update.** The email commits to writing again in February with how many children started lessons. Only send it if you'll do that. For this group, keeping that promise matters as much as this email does.\n- **The match terms.** Confirm with the foundation what counts as a \"returning donor.\" For example, does someone who last gave in 2018 qualify?\n- **The figures.** $170 pays for about 7 weeks of lessons, so the email says \"nearly two months.\" $575 doubled covers one child's full year.\n\n<final_document>\n**Subject:** 61 kids are waiting. This month, your gift counts double.\n\nDear [First name],\n\nYou used to give to [School name], and I want to start by thanking you. You helped put instruments in kids' hands.\n\nI also know many of you stepped away after we closed our Eastside branch in 2022. Some of you told us how much that hurt, and you had every right to. We haven't forgotten it.\n\nHere is where things stand. Right now, 61 children are on our waiting list for subsidized lessons. A year of weekly lessons costs us $1,150 per child.\n\nThis December, a family foundation will match every gift from returning donors dollar for dollar, up to $15,000. That means:\n\n- **$85 becomes $170:** nearly two months of weekly lessons for one child.\n- **$575 becomes $1,150:** a full year of lessons for one child.\n\nThe match ends December 31, or sooner if we reach $15,000.\n\nI can't promise that every child on the list will have a place in January. I can promise you this: in February, I'll write to tell you exactly how many of those 61 children started lessons, and what your gift made possible.\n\nIf you're willing to come back, this is the month when your gift goes furthest.\n\n**[Give now: doubled through December 31]**\n\nWith gratitude,\n\n[Executive Director name]\nExecutive Director, [School name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5419,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5419},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24f4bb87-24ee-484e-b43c-8b0c065a3726","uuid":"8dbf2324-9779-4a48-b60a-d21df4a9c829","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:01:04.224Z","request_id":"req_011Ch73Vvgg7DnPmUhVk6Za5"}
